# 🏢 2. Active Directory

## 2.1 Domain Controller

A Domain Controller (DC) is a server that hosts Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS).

It provides functions such as:

* Authentication
* Directory services
* Domain-related management
* User and computer authentication

### Basic Flow

```text
User
 ↓
Domain Controller
 ↓
Authentication
 ↓
Domain Resources
```

### Important Distinction

```text
Domain
↓
Logical environment

Active Directory Domain Services
↓
Directory service

Domain Controller
↓
Server that hosts AD DS
```

---

# 2.2 Computer Account

A computer account is an Active Directory object that represents a computer joined to the domain.

Example:

```text
Computer:
PC-FIN-001

        ↓

Active Directory
        ↓
Computer Account
```

Computer accounts allow the organization to manage domain-joined computers.

---

# 2.3 Domain Join

Domain joining adds a computer to an Active Directory domain.

### Basic Process

```text
Computer
 ↓
Correct DNS configuration
 ↓
Reach Domain Controller
 ↓
Authorized domain credentials
 ↓
Join Domain
 ↓
Restart
 ↓
Domain Authentication
```

### Important

Incorrect DNS configuration can prevent domain-join operations because the computer needs to locate domain services and Domain Controllers.

---

# 2.4 GPO Inheritance

Group Policy settings can be inherited from higher-level Active Directory containers and may affect lower-level OUs and objects depending on the policy configuration and processing rules.

### Basic Structure

```text
Domain
 ↓
OU
 ↓
Sub-OU
 ↓
User / Computer
```

### Interview Answer

> GPO inheritance allows policy settings from higher-level Active Directory containers to be inherited by lower-level containers and objects according to Group Policy processing rules.

